<title>USA: BankBoston issues employee stock option.</title>
<headline>BankBoston issues employee stock option.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankBoston said Friday it has issued a performance-based stock option award to 22,000 full- and part-time employees.</p>
<p>The option is to be based on BankBoston's closing stock price on October 1 to employees who have not previously received a stock award in 1996.</p>
<p>The number of options awarded to each employee will be either 10 percent of their base pay divided by the October 1 closing stock price, or 100 shares for full-time employees and 50 shares for part-time employees, whichever is greater.  </p>
<p>The grant allows employees to exercise 75 percent of their options after the company's stock price reaches either $60 or $65 per share, depending on the October 1 closing price, it said.</p>
